# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches a directory only, so
# a *symlink* named node_modules — which is how a git worktree borrows the real
# tree's install — slips past it and gets committed. That happened on
# 2026-08-16: the branch carried a symlink whose content was an absolute path on
# one machine, pointing at itself once checked out there, and every `tsc` after
# that died with "too many levels of symbolic links". `npm run build` exits 216
# and prints NOTHING, so the suite silently ran against a stale `dist/`.
node_modules
dist/

# Carries the GitHub credential. The negation keeps the template tracked —
# without it, adding .env.* silently untracks the one file here meant to be
# committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# The GitHub App private key. It signs the JWT that mints installation tokens,
# so a copy in the tree is a copy of every permission the app has.
*.pem
*.private-key.pem

# Local state, if you point paths.stateFile at the working directory rather
# than /var/lib/oj while developing.
state.json
workers/
